  "title": "A Certified Zero-Free Interval Through 1024 for the Golden-Mean Fourier Transform",
  "batch_label": "70",
  "kind": "result-note",
  "original_status": "unresolved",
  "scope": "For the self-similar measure mu and Fourier transform F fixed in source.md and problem.md, F(xi) is nonzero for every real xi satisfying 27/25 <= |xi| <= 1024. This is a strict subsidiary theorem and does not settle the frozen assertion for 1024 < |xi| <= 10^7.",
